{
  "_comment": [
    "Secret redaction rules, shared by the hook (core/bin/prepare.jq) and the sender (judgment_core/redact.py). This file is the source.",
    "scripts/gen_redact.py derives core/bin/redact-compiled.json (what jq loads: every regex composed) from it.",
    "Regexes use what Oniguruma and Python re agree on: (?<name>...) for a named group (p: the text it holds is kept);",
    "no ^ or $ (use (?<![\\s\\S]) and (?![\\s\\S]) for the ends of a whole value); [0-9] and [A-Za-z], not \\d and \\w;",
    "no (?i), because Oniguruma compiles it slowly and jq compiles a regex on every call. Words are spelled lower, UPPER, and Capitalized.",
    "Every repeat a lookahead scans is bounded, so no input makes a rule rescan the text after it (tests/test_latency.py).",
    "needs: a rule can match only text holding one of these literals. Both layers skip the regex otherwise. tests/test_redact.py checks it.",
    "pre: a small regex every match also matches; both layers skip the rule's regex when the text does not match it (a cheap",
    "filter before an expensive regex). tests/test_redact.py checks it the way it checks needs."
  ],
  "version": 3,
  "defs": {
    "_comment": [
      "Regex fragments rules share. A rule's re may be a list: strings, and {\"def\": name} for one of these, or {\"gen\": name} for a",
      "fragment scripts/gen_redact.py and redact.py compose from the tables below (secret_keys, literals).",
      "secret_value: an unquoted value that looks like a credential. Not a reference (${X}, os.environ, process.env, a.b.c member),",
      "a placeholder, a versioned name (api_key_v2), or a constant (API_KEY_2024, DEFAULT_PASSWORD2: CAPITAL words joined by _, or one",
      "CAPITAL word with up to 4 digits), which in code name a value rather than hold one."
    ],
    "secret_name": "(?:api|API|Api)[_-]?(?:key|KEY|Key)|(?:secret|SECRET|Secret)[_-]?(?:key|KEY|Key)|(?:client|CLIENT|Client)[_-]?(?:secret|SECRET|Secret)|(?:secret|SECRET|Secret)|(?:access|ACCESS|Access)[_-]?(?:key|KEY|Key)|(?:private|PRIVATE|Private)[_-]?(?:key|KEY|Key)|(?:auth|AUTH|Auth)[_-]?(?:token|TOKEN|Token)|(?:access|ACCESS|Access)[_-]?(?:token|TOKEN|Token)|(?:refresh|REFRESH|Refresh)[_-]?(?:token|TOKEN|Token)|(?:session|SESSION|Session)[_-]?(?:token|TOKEN|Token)|(?:token|TOKEN|Token)|(?:password|PASSWORD|Password)|(?:passwd|PASSWD|Passwd)|(?:passphrase|PASSPHRASE|Passphrase)|(?:credentials|CREDENTIALS|Credentials)|(?:credential|CREDENTIAL|Credential)",
    "secret_value": "(?!\\\\?[\\\"']?(?:xxx|XXX|Xxx|\\*\\*\\*|\\.\\.\\.|changeme|CHANGEME|Changeme|change_me|CHANGE_ME|Change_me|change-me|CHANGE-ME|Change-me|your_|YOUR_|Your_|your-|YOUR-|Your-|example|EXAMPLE|Example|placeholder|PLACEHOLDER|Placeholder|dummy|DUMMY|Dummy|redacted|REDACTED|Redacted|sample|SAMPLE|Sample|null\\b|NULL\\B|Null\\b|none\\b|NONE\\B|None\\b|undefined\\b|UNDEFINED\\B|Undefined\\b|true\\b|TRUE\\B|True\\b|false\\b|FALSE\\B|False\\b|process\\.env|PROCESS\\.ENV|Process\\.env|os\\.environ|OS\\.ENVIRON|Os\\.environ|os\\.getenv|OS\\.GETENV|Os\\.getenv|env\\.|ENV\\.|Env\\.|env\\[|ENV\\[|Env\\[|getenv|GETENV|Getenv|secrets\\.|SECRETS\\.|Secrets\\.|vault:|VAULT:|Vault:|arn:|ARN:|Arn:))(?![A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,63}(?:\\.[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,63}){1,16}(?![A-Za-z0-9_\\-+/.~!@#%^*]))(?![A-Za-z_]{1,64}_?[vV][0-9]{1,3}(?![A-Za-z0-9_\\-+/.~!@#%^*]))(?![A-Z][A-Z0-9]{0,63}(?:_[A-Z0-9]{1,63}){1,8}(?![A-Za-z0-9_\\-+/.~!@#%^*]))(?![A-Z]{2,64}[0-9]{1,4}(?![A-Za-z0-9_\\-+/.~!@#%^*]))(?![$<{%\\[(/~.])(?=[A-Za-z0-9_\\-+/.~!@#%^*]{0,255}[0-9])(?=[A-Za-z0-9_\\-+/.~!@#%^*]{0,255}[A-Za-z])[A-Za-z0-9_\\-+/.~!@#%^*]{8,256}={0,3}(?=[\\\"'`\\s,;)}\\]&<>|\\\\]|$)",
    "secret_key": "[A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,64}?(?:(?:api|API|Api)[_-]?(?:key|KEY|Key)|(?:secret|SECRET|Secret)[_-]?(?:key|KEY|Key)|(?:client|CLIENT|Client)[_-]?(?:secret|SECRET|Secret)|(?:secret|SECRET|Secret)|(?:access|ACCESS|Access)[_-]?(?:key|KEY|Key)|(?:private|PRIVATE|Private)[_-]?(?:key|KEY|Key)|(?:auth|AUTH|Auth)[_-]?(?:token|TOKEN|Token)|(?:access|ACCESS|Access)[_-]?(?:token|TOKEN|Token)|(?:refresh|REFRESH|Refresh)[_-]?(?:token|TOKEN|Token)|(?:session|SESSION|Session)[_-]?(?:token|TOKEN|Token)|(?:token|TOKEN|Token)|(?:password|PASSWORD|Password)|(?:passwd|PASSWD|Passwd)|(?:passphrase|PASSPHRASE|Passphrase)|(?:credentials|CREDENTIALS|Credentials)|(?:credential|CREDENTIAL|Credential))"
  },
  "limits": {
    "_comment": [
      "Bounds on the work redaction does, so no input makes the hook slow (tests/test_latency.py).",
      "A rule runs over windows of the unchanged text: each `window` characters long, one every `step`. jq's global match counts each",
      "match's offset from the start of the string it is given, so short strings keep that linear. Text no longer than `window` is one",
      "window. A match is kept from every window that holds it whole. A match that reaches the end of a window that is not the last is",
      "seen whole by the next window when it starts at or after that window's start; when it starts before, it is longer than",
      "window - step characters and the event fails closed. A rule marked whole runs over all of the text, and fails when the text holds",
      "more than `most` of the literals it needs. More than `pairs` distinct finds in one event fail too, as does a prompt with more than",
      "`mentions` @ signs. A failure drops the event's text, as an invalid user regex does.",
      "A window of at most `dense` characters is matched globally (one regex compile; few enough matches that jq's offset counting",
      "costs little). A longer one is matched one distinct match at a time, each one's copies blanked first, so repeats cost one search."
    ],
    "window": 16384,
    "step": 8192,
    "pairs": 128,
    "mentions": 256,
    "dense": 8192
  },
  "patterns": [
    {
      "id": "private_key",
      "needs": [
        "PRIVATE KEY"
      ],
      "re": "-----BEGIN[A-Z0-9 ]{0,30}PRIVATE KEY(?: BLOCK)?-----(?:[\\s\\S]{0,16384}?-----END[A-Z0-9 ]{0,30}PRIVATE KEY(?: BLOCK)?-----|[A-Za-z0-9+/=\\s\\\\:,-]{0,16384})",
      "whole": true,
      "most": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "jwt",
      "needs": [
        "eyJ"
      ],
      "re": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,}\\.eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]*"
    },
    {
      "id": "anthropic_key",
      "needs": [
        "sk-ant-"
      ],
      "re": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])sk-ant-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}"
    },
    {
      "id": "openai_key",
      "needs": [
        "sk-"
      ],
      "re": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])sk-(?:proj-|svcacct-|admin-)?(?=[A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,256}?[A-Za-z0-9_]{16})[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}",
      "pre": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])sk-"
    },
    {
      "id": "aws_access_key_id",
      "needs": [
        "AKIA",
        "ASIA",
        "ABIA",
        "ACCA"
      ],
      "re": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9])(?:AKIA|ASIA|ABIA|ACCA)[0-9A-Z]{16}(?![0-9A-Za-z])"
    },
    {
      "id": "github_token",
      "needs": [
        "ghp_",
        "gho_",
        "ghu_",
        "ghs_",
        "ghr_"
      ],
      "re": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])gh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{36,}"
    },
    {
      "id": "github_pat",
      "needs": [
        "github_pat_"
      ],
      "re": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])github_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{22,}"
    },
    {
      "id": "slack_token",
      "needs": [
        "xoxa-",
        "xoxb-",
        "xoxp-",
        "xoxr-",
        "xoxs-",
        "xoxe-"
      ],
      "re": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])xox[abprse]-(?=[A-Za-z0-9-]{0,255}[0-9])[A-Za-z0-9-]{10,}"
    },
    {
      "id": "slack_webhook",
      "needs": [
        "hooks.slack.com/services/"
      ],
      "re": "(?<p>hooks\\.slack\\.com/services/)[A-Za-z0-9/_-]{20,}"
    },
    {
      "id": "google_api_key",
      "needs": [
        "AIza"
      ],
      "re": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])AIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]{35}(?![0-9A-Za-z_-])"
    },
    {
      "id": "stripe_key",
      "needs": [
        "sk_live_",
        "sk_test_",
        "rk_live_",
        "rk_test_"
      ],
      "re": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])(?:sk|rk)_(?:live|test)_[A-Za-z0-9]{16,}"
    },
    {
      "id": "url_password",
      "needs": [
        "://"
      ],
      "re": "(?<p>(?<![A-Za-z0-9+.-])[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.-]{1,20}://[^\\s/:@'\\\"<>\\[\\]]{1,128}:)(?!\\[REDACTED|\\$\\{|\\$[A-Za-z_(]|<|\\{\\{|%|\\*+@|x+@|(?:password|PASSWORD|Password|pass|PASS|Pass|passwd|PASSWD|Passwd|pwd|PWD|Pwd|secret|SECRET|Secret|changeme|CHANGEME|Changeme)@)[^\\s/@'\\\"<>]{3,256}(?=@)"
    },
    {
      "id": "authorization_header",
      "needs": [
        "uthorization",
        "UTHORIZATION",
        "-key",
        "-Key",
        "-KEY",
        "-token",
        "-Token",
        "-TOKEN"
      ],
      "re": "(?<p>(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])(?:(?:proxy|PROXY|Proxy)-(?:authorization|AUTHORIZATION|Authorization)|(?:authorization|AUTHORIZATION|Authorization)|(?:x|X)-(?:api|API|Api)-(?:key|KEY|Key)|(?:api|API|Api)-(?:key|KEY|Key)|(?:x|X)-(?:auth|AUTH|Auth)-(?:token|TOKEN|Token))\\\\?[\\\"']?\\s{0,5}[:=]\\s{0,5}\\\\?[\\\"']?(?:(?:basic|BASIC|Basic|bearer|BEARER|Bearer|token|TOKEN|Token|digest|DIGEST|Digest|bot|BOT|Bot|apikey|APIKEY|Apikey)\\s+)?)(?!\\$|<|\\{\\{|%)(?=[A-Za-z._~+/=-]{0,255}[0-9+/=])[A-Za-z0-9._~+/=-]{12,}"
    },
    {
      "id": "bearer_token",
      "needs": [
        "bearer",
        "BEARER",
        "Bearer"
      ],
      "re": "(?<p>(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])(?:bearer|BEARER|Bearer)\\s+)(?!\\$|<|\\{\\{|%)(?=[A-Za-z._~+/=-]{0,255}[0-9])[A-Za-z0-9._~+/=-]{16,}"
    },
    {
      "id": "secret_assignment",
      "needs": [
        "key",
        "KEY",
        "Key",
        "secret",
        "SECRET",
        "Secret",
        "token",
        "TOKEN",
        "Token",
        "password",
        "PASSWORD",
        "Password",
        "passwd",
        "PASSWD",
        "Passwd",
        "passphrase",
        "PASSPHRASE",
        "Passphrase",
        "credential",
        "CREDENTIAL",
        "Credential"
      ],
      "re": [
        "(?<p>(?:",
        {
          "def": "secret_name"
        },
        ")\\\\?[\\\"']?\\s{0,5}(?::=|=>|[:=])\\s{0,5}\\\\?[\\\"']?)",
        {
          "def": "secret_value"
        }
      ],
      "pre": "(?:key|KEY|Key|secret|SECRET|Secret|token|TOKEN|Token|password|PASSWORD|Password|passwd|PASSWD|Passwd|passphrase|PASSPHRASE|Passphrase|credentials|CREDENTIALS|Credentials|credential|CREDENTIAL|Credential)\\\\?[\"']?\\s{0,5}(?::=|=>|[:=])"
    },
    {
      "id": "quoted_secret",
      "needs": "secret_key_name",
      "re": [
        "(?<p>(?:",
        {
          "gen": "secret_key_tail"
        },
        ")\\\\?[\"']?\\s{0,5}(?::=|=>|[:=])\\s{0,5}(?:\\\\\"|\"|'))",
        "(?!(?:",
        {
          "gen": "literal"
        },
        ")(?:\\\\\"|\"|'))",
        "(?:(?<=\\\\\")[^\"\\\\\\n]{1,256}(?=\\\\\")|(?<=\")(?:[^\"\\\\\\n]|\\\\[^\\n]){1,256}(?=\")|(?<=')(?:[^'\\\\\\n]|\\\\[^\\n]){1,256}(?='))"
      ],
      "pre": [
        "(?:",
        {
          "gen": "secret_key_last"
        },
        ")\\\\?[\"']?\\s{0,5}(?::=|=>|[:=])\\s{0,5}\\\\?[\"']"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "env": {
    "_comment": [
      "The value of each environment variable whose name looks secret is replaced literally wherever it appears: the whole value,",
      "and each line of a value that spans lines. name_re runs over the names, one per line, and matches each secret name whole.",
      "A name matches when it is JUDGMENT_API_KEY, or holds KEY, TOKEN, SECRET, PASSWORD, PASSWD, CREDENTIAL, PRIVATE, or AUTH",
      "(not as part of AUTHOR, KEYBOARD, KEYMAP, KEYCHAIN, MONKEY, TURKEY), and does not end in a suffix that names a location or a",
      "setting (_PATH, _FILE, _DIR, _SOCK, _URL, _HOST, _ID, _TOKENS, _LIMIT, ...): those values are paths, hosts, ids, or numbers.",
      "Any value (or line) of min_length or more characters with something other than whitespace in it is replaced, whatever its",
      "shape. A shorter one is not: replacing every 4-character run such as 2024 in all text would destroy ordinary text. Known limit."
    ],
    "name_re": "(?<![^\\n])(?:JUDGMENT_API_KEY(?![^\\n])|(?=[^\\n]*?(?:token|TOKEN|Token|secret|SECRET|Secret|password|PASSWORD|Password|passwd|PASSWD|Passwd|credential|CREDENTIAL|Credential|private|PRIVATE|Private|auth(?!or(?!iz))|AUTH(?!OR(?!IZ))|Auth(?!or(?!iz))|(?<![Mm][Oo][Nn])(?<![Tt][Uu][Rr])(?:key|KEY|Key)(?![Bb][Oo][Aa][Rr][Dd]|[Mm][Aa][Pp]|[Cc][Hh][Aa][Ii][Nn])))(?![^\\n]*(?:_PATH|_path|_FILE|_file|_DIR|_dir|_SOCK|_sock|_SOCKET|_socket|_HOST|_host|_PORT|_port|_URL|_url|_URI|_uri|_ID|_id|_MODE|_mode|_TYPE|_type|_NAME|_name|_USER|_user|_USERNAME|_username|_ENABLED|_enabled|_DISABLED|_disabled|_TIMEOUT|_timeout|_TOKENS|_tokens|_LIMIT|_limit|_REGION|_region)(?![^\\n]))[^\\n]+)",
    "min_length": 8
  },
  "sensitive": {
    "_comment": [
      "A tool call that reads one of these paths, or dumps the environment, blanks its whole turn.",
      "keys: the tool input members whose string (or list of strings) values are paths or commands, at any depth.",
      "split: the characters that end a word of those values. Path rules see one word per line. Command rules see the values, one per line.",
      "mention: an @word in the prompt is a path too. A word starts after one of mention.split and ends at one of mention.end.",
      "glob: how a redactPaths glob becomes a regex, one character at a time. * is any run of characters, / included, and ? is one."
    ],
    "paths": [
      {
        "id": "dotenv",
        "needs": [
          ".env"
        ],
        "re": "(?<![^\\n/])\\.env(?:rc)?(?:[.*](?!(?:example|sample|template|dist|defaults?|schema)(?![^\\n]))(?:[A-Za-z0-9_.*-]|\\[REDACTED:[^\\]\\n]{1,128}\\])*)?(?![^\\n])"
      },
      {
        "id": "ssh_private_key",
        "needs": [
          "id_rsa",
          "id_dsa",
          "id_ecdsa",
          "id_ed25519"
        ],
        "re": "(?<![^\\n/])id_(?:rsa|dsa|ecdsa|ed25519)(?:_sk)?(?![^\\n])"
      },
      {
        "id": "key_file",
        "needs": [
          ".pem",
          ".key",
          ".p12",
          ".pfx",
          ".jks",
          ".keystore",
          ".ppk"
        ],
        "re": "(?<![^\\n/])[^\\n/]*[A-Za-z0-9_-]\\.(?:pem|key|p12|pfx|jks|keystore|ppk)(?![^\\n])"
      },
      {
        "id": "credentials_file",
        "needs": [
          "credentials"
        ],
        "re": "(?:(?<=/)credentials|(?<![^\\n/])[A-Za-z0-9_.-]*credentials\\.(?:json|ya?ml|toml|ini|csv|xml|db))(?![^\\n])"
      },
      {
        "id": "secret_file",
        "needs": [
          "secret",
          "SECRET",
          "Secret"
        ],
        "re": "(?<![^\\n/])(?=[^\\n/]*\\.)(?![^\\n/]*\\.(?:py|pyi|js|mjs|cjs|ts|tsx|jsx|go|rs|java|kt|rb|php|cs|c|h|cc|cpp|hpp|swift|scala|sh|bash|zsh|ps1|md|mdx|rst|html|css|scss|sql|proto|lock|map|snap|svg|png|jpg|ipynb)(?![^\\n]))[^\\n/]*(?:secret|SECRET|Secret)[^\\n/]*(?![^\\n])"
      },
      {
        "id": "auth_file",
        "needs": [
          "netrc",
          "npmrc",
          "pypirc",
          "git-credentials",
          "pgpass",
          "htpasswd",
          "dockercfg",
          "auth.json",
          ".boto",
          "s3cfg",
          "vault-token",
          "config"
        ],
        "re": "(?:(?<![^\\n/])(?:\\.netrc|_netrc|\\.npmrc|\\.pypirc|\\.git-credentials|\\.pgpass|\\.htpasswd|\\.dockercfg|auth\\.json|\\.boto|\\.s3cfg|\\.vault-token)|(?<=\\.docker/)config\\.json|(?<=\\.kube/)config)(?![^\\n])"
      },
      {
        "id": "proc_environ",
        "needs": [
          "/environ"
        ],
        "re": "(?<![^\\n])/proc/[^\\n/]+/environ(?![^\\n])"
      }
    ],
    "commands": [
      {
        "id": "env_dump",
        "needs": [
          "env",
          "set",
          "export",
          "declare",
          "typeset"
        ],
        "re": "(?<![^\\n;&|(`])\\s*(?:sudo\\s+)?(?:(?:/[^\\s;&|()`/]{1,64}){0,8}/)?(?:env(?:\\s+(?:-[uCS]\\s+[^\\s;&|)>`-][^\\s;&|)>`]{0,255}|-[A-Za-z0-9-]{1,32}(?:=[^\\s;&|)>`]{0,255})?|[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,63}=[^\\s;&|)>`]{0,255})){0,16}|printenv|set|export|export\\s+-p|declare\\s+-[a-z]*[px][a-z]*|typeset\\s+-[a-z]*x[a-z]*)\\s*(?![^\\n;&|)>`])"
      },
      {
        "id": "printenv",
        "needs": [
          "printenv"
        ],
        "re": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])printenv(?![A-Za-z0-9_-])"
      },
      {
        "id": "credentials_file",
        "needs": [
          "credentials"
        ],
        "re": "(?:(?<![^\\n;&|(`])\\s*(?:sudo\\s+)?(?:cat|less|more|head|tail|bat|batcat|tac|nl|xxd|od|strings|base64|source|vi|vim|nvim|nano|emacs|code|open|cp|scp|rsync|type|Get-Content)(?:\\s+[^\\s;&|<>()`]{1,256}){0,16}?\\s+[\"']?|(?<![^\\n]))(?:\\./)?credentials(?![^\\s;&|)>`'\"])"
      },
      {
        "id": "secret_cli",
        "needs": [
          "gh",
          "aws",
          "git",
          "gcloud",
          "security",
          "op",
          "vault",
          "kubectl"
        ],
        "re": "(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])(?:gh\\s+auth\\s+token|aws\\s+configure\\s+(?:get|export-credentials)|git\\s+credential\\s+fill|gcloud\\s+auth\\s+(?:application-default\\s+)?print-(?:access|identity)-token|security\\s+find-(?:generic|internet)-password|op\\s+read|vault\\s+(?:read|kv\\s+get)|kubectl\\s+(?:get|describe|edit)\\s+secrets?)(?![A-Za-z0-9_-])"
      }
    ],
    "keys": {
      "file_path": true,
      "filePath": true,
      "path": true,
      "paths": true,
      "file": true,
      "files": true,
      "filename": true,
      "notebook_path": true,
      "target_file": true,
      "target_notebook": true,
      "absolute_path": true,
      "relative_path": true,
      "source": true,
      "destination": true,
      "command": true,
      "cmd": true,
      "commands": true,
      "script": true
    },
    "glob": {
      "*": "[^\\n]*",
      "?": "[^\\n]",
      ".": "\\.",
      "\\": "\\\\",
      "+": "\\+",
      "^": "\\^",
      "$": "\\$",
      "(": "\\(",
      ")": "\\)",
      "[": "\\[",
      "]": "\\]",
      "{": "\\{",
      "}": "\\}",
      "|": "\\|"
    },
    "split": [
      " ",
      "\t",
      "\n",
      "\r",
      "\f",
      "\u000b",
      "\"",
      "'",
      "`",
      ";",
      "|",
      "&",
      "<",
      ">",
      "(",
      ")",
      "="
    ],
    "mention": {
      "split": [
        " ",
        "\t",
        "\n",
        "\r",
        "\f",
        "\u000b",
        "("
      ],
      "end": [
        ",",
        ";",
        ")"
      ]
    }
  },
  "fields": {
    "_comment": [
      "The class of each event field. A field not listed is text.",
      "strip: kept when an event loses its text (metadata capture at the hook, a sensitive event, a rule error, a blanked turn).",
      "redact: secrets in it are replaced. metadata: kept by metadata capture once transcripts were read.",
      "drop_when_blanked: dropped from the events a blanked turn's spans are built from, so a free-form name cannot become a span name."
    ],
    "classes": {
      "keep": {
        "strip": true,
        "redact": false,
        "metadata": true
      },
      "transport": {
        "strip": true,
        "redact": false,
        "metadata": false
      },
      "label": {
        "strip": true,
        "redact": true,
        "metadata": true
      },
      "text_label": {
        "strip": false,
        "redact": true,
        "metadata": false,
        "drop_when_blanked": true
      },
      "text": {
        "strip": false,
        "redact": true,
        "metadata": false
      }
    },
    "of": {
      "v": "keep",
      "kind": "keep",
      "name": "keep",
      "harness": "keep",
      "harness_version": "keep",
      "event": "keep",
      "session_id": "keep",
