  "secret_keys": {
    "_comment": [
      "Keys and names that hold a secret whatever the value looks like. A word is lowercase parts joined by _; it matches lower, UPPER,",
      "and Capitalized parts joined by _, -, ., or nothing (api_key, API-KEY, apiKey, ApiKey). names match as the whole key, or as its",
      "end after a separator or a camelCase boundary (db_password, smtpPassword, X-Api-Key). whole match only as the whole key.",
      "Generic words are left out on purpose: token, key, auth (max_tokens, token_count, tokenizer, sort_key). Those keep the shape test.",
      "A structured member {\"<key>\": \"<string>\"} under such a key loses any nonempty string value but a reference or placeholder",
      "(literals below); booleans, numbers, and null stay. In text, <name> = \"<quoted>\" loses the quoted value the same way."
    ],
    "names": [
      "password",
      "passwd",
      "passphrase",
      "secret",
      "api_key",
      "api_secret",
      "api_token",
      "access_token",
      "refresh_token",
      "auth_token",
      "id_token",
      "session_token",
      "bearer_token",
      "private_key",
      "secret_key",
      "secret_access_key",
      "signing_key",
      "encryption_key",
      "master_key"
    ],
    "whole": [
      "pwd",
      "apikey",
      "authorization",
      "proxy_authorization",
      "credential",
      "credentials"
    ]
  },
  "literals": {
    "_comment": [
      "Values under a secret key that are not secrets: references and placeholders, matched against the whole value as JSON",
      "escapes it (so \" is \\\", which these never hold). refs: start-anchored, the rest of the value is anything. words: whole value,",
      "in lower, UPPER, and Capitalized. forms: whole value, regex."
    ],
    "refs": [
      "\\$\\{",
      "\\$[A-Za-z_]",
      "\\{\\{",
      "\\{%",
      "%\\(",
      "process\\.env",
      "os\\.environ",
      "os\\.getenv",
      "getenv\\(",
      "ENV\\[",
      "secrets\\.",
      "vault:",
      "op://",
      "arn:aws:secretsmanager:",
      "\\[REDACTED"
    ],
    "words": [
      "changeme",
      "change_me",
      "change-me",
      "placeholder",
      "dummy",
      "example",
      "sample",
      "redacted",
      "secret",
      "password",
      "null",
      "none",
      "nil",
      "undefined",
      "true",
      "false",
      "todo",
      "tbd"
    ],
    "forms": [
      "x{3,}",
      "X{3,}",
      "\\*{3,}",
      "\\.{3,}",
      "<[^<>\"\\\\\\n]{1,128}>",
      "%[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,63}%",
      "(?:your|YOUR|Your)[_-][A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,128}"
    ]
  },
  "members": [
    {
      "_comment": [
        "A member under a secret key (secret_keys) loses any nonempty string value but a reference or placeholder (literals).",
        "json_re runs over the compact JSON of the event's text fields in both layers, as jq writes it."
      ],
      "id": "secret_field",
      "json_re": [
        "(?<p>(?<=[{,])\"(?:",
        {
          "gen": "secret_key_name"
        },
        ")\":\")(?!(?:",
        {
          "gen": "literal"
        },
        ")\")(?:[^\"\\\\]|\\\\.)+(?=\")"
      ],
      "needs": "secret_key_name",
      "needs_suffix": "\":\""
    },
    {
      "_comment": [
        "A member whose key ends in a secret word, and whose string value looks like a secret, loses its value (the shape test).",
        "secret_assignment sees `key = value` in text. This sees {\"token\": value} in structured tool input and output.",
        "secret_value has no quote or backslash, so a value matches the same escaped or not."
      ],
      "id": "secret_field",
      "needs": [
        "key\":\"",
        "KEY\":\"",
        "Key\":\"",
        "secret\":\"",
        "SECRET\":\"",
        "Secret\":\"",
        "token\":\"",
        "TOKEN\":\"",
        "Token\":\"",
        "password\":\"",
        "PASSWORD\":\"",
        "Password\":\"",
        "passwd\":\"",
        "PASSWD\":\"",
        "Passwd\":\"",
        "passphrase\":\"",
        "PASSPHRASE\":\"",
        "Passphrase\":\"",
        "credential\":\"",
        "CREDENTIAL\":\"",
        "Credential\":\"",
        "credentials\":\"",
        "CREDENTIALS\":\"",
        "Credentials\":\""
      ],
      "json_re": [
        "(?<p>(?<=[{,])\"",
        {
          "def": "secret_key"
        },
        "\":\")",
        {
          "def": "secret_value"
        },
        "(?=\")"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "members_comment": [
    "Structured members, as {\"key\":\"value\"} in the compact JSON of each event's text fields, in order: the secret key",
    "tier, then the shape tier. Both are the rule secret_field. needs \"secret_key_name\": the last word of each secret key name."
  ]
}
